**Read:** [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), the complete gravity-concentration and relevant particle/fluid chapters; [Tratamento de Minérios: Práticas Laboratoriais — Sampaio, França, and Braga](../sources/CETEM-Praticas-Laboratoriais.lingua#r_44AAWXB1D7MBR9B0V3TYB8GF9B), the full applicable gravity test methods; [Introduction to Mineral Processing — Arun Kumar Majumder, NPTEL](../sources/Introduction-to-Mineral-Processing-NPTEL.lingua#r_5VQ67PA1160RQ1EWN17211XBWD), the complete movement-in-fluids and gravity sequence.

Gravity concentration exploits differences in particle response under gravity/flow or an applied acceleration field. Density, size, shape, mineral association, fluid properties, crowding, and equipment motion/geometry influence behavior. A density contrast alone does not establish a sharp or economically useful split.

Simple settling laws require defined regimes and assumptions. Laminar isolated-sphere, turbulent, hindered-settling, and concentrated-flow accounts differ. Applying a convenient formula across all sizes/shapes/concentrations without checking conditions can reverse a selectivity inference.

Jigs, tables, spirals, centrifugal devices, and other methods create different flow/force histories and constraints. Product yield, grade, recovery, mineral loss by size, and throughput must be assessed together. Fine intergrowth or a size-density tradeoff can limit performance despite attractive bulk density data.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete gravity-separation lab/plant case with feed association and size/density populations. Independently check material/constituent balances and one motion/selectivity model within its stated range. Compare a plausible feed or operating-history alternative and identify the discriminating test.

Read full theory/lab chapters and primary method used. Later specialist fluid/particle and processing work deepens the mechanisms while reusing this material/measurement account and the observation limits.

**Continue:** [Evaluate dense-media concentration with the medium and particle populations explicit](Dense-media-separation-medium-control-and-material-response.lingua#r_5JP09XGADZNJ6YZ5QTY6Y5E9RN).

